1
00:00:00,320 --> 00:00:03,750
It's seven in the morning and these people
have been walking since midnight.

2
00:00:03,800 --> 00:00:07,350
13 kilometres along the coast of Kerala,
praying the rosary without ever stopping.

3
00:00:12,780 --> 00:00:16,850
In 1647 a statue of Saint Sebastian
arrives from Milan.

4
00:00:17,590 --> 00:00:19,250
The world, told by those who live it.

5
00:00:19,800 --> 00:00:21,900
This is Voci Vere.

6
00:00:23,420 --> 00:00:25,750
It's called Akhanda Japamala, the unbroken
rosary.

7
00:00:26,450 --> 00:00:28,600
It starts from a shrine dedicated to Mary,
in Kalavoor,

8
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:30,800
and it ends in Arthunkal.

9
00:00:31,240 --> 00:00:33,900
13 kilometres along the coast, and the
prayer never stops.

10
00:00:41,633 --> 00:00:43,633
No one would have guessed it would fill up
during the night.

11
00:00:53,543 --> 00:00:55,583
We set off in the dark, no one talks about
anything else.

12
00:00:56,133 --> 00:00:59,383
Whoever leads the rosary says the first
half of the prayer. The others answer.

13
00:00:59,433 --> 00:01:00,633
For kilometres.

14
00:01:01,193 --> 00:01:03,883
The prayer passes from one group to the
next, without a gap.

15
00:01:09,533 --> 00:01:11,183
Hundreds of thousands of people.

16
00:01:11,613 --> 00:01:14,183
The first time, in 2002, there were a few
hundred.

17
00:01:14,653 --> 00:01:18,133
As they told us, it starts from a shrine
dedicated to Mary, in Kalavoor.

18
00:01:18,573 --> 00:01:21,433
They used to do it all on the road, but
with the traffic

19
00:01:21,533 --> 00:01:24,733
it got too chaotic, so they moved straight
onto the beach.

20
00:01:25,503 --> 00:01:27,133
Some come for faith, some for a promise,

21
00:01:27,573 --> 00:01:28,633
some because their father did it before
them.

22
00:01:29,123 --> 00:01:30,533
The road is the same for everyone.

23
00:01:31,483 --> 00:01:32,683
What does it mean for you?

24
00:01:32,933 --> 00:01:35,833
So this is basically a rally which happens
every year.

25
00:01:36,433 --> 00:01:39,333
It's based on the apparition of Mother
Mary

26
00:01:39,333 --> 00:01:40,933
which happened in Alappuzha.

27
00:01:41,433 --> 00:01:43,433
It happened in December 2004,

28
00:01:44,333 --> 00:01:45,433
December seventh, I guess,

29
00:01:45,533 --> 00:01:49,433
at 2:30 in the afternoon: an apparition of
Mother Mary.

30
00:01:50,333 --> 00:01:56,433
October is the month of the Rosary, for
Mother Mary.

31
00:01:56,733 --> 00:01:59,233
We celebrate it with a big rally.

32
00:02:00,233 --> 00:02:02,133
It ends at the Basilica of Saint Andrew.

33
00:02:03,333 --> 00:02:07,683
Since October is the month of Mother Mary,
we dedicate this month to the rally.

34
00:02:08,233 --> 00:02:11,183
And about four lakh people take part in
it.

35
00:02:11,633 --> 00:02:12,233
How many people?

36
00:02:12,283 --> 00:02:14,033
Four lakh. Close to four lakh.

37
00:02:16,533 --> 00:02:18,383
Can you tell me why you do it?

38
00:02:19,333 --> 00:02:24,183
It's like a prayer to Jesus, my love.

39
00:02:24,383 --> 00:02:26,183
It's like... for one year.

40
00:02:26,933 --> 00:02:27,683
One time.

41
00:02:31,633 --> 00:02:33,783
Why do you come back every year?

42
00:02:33,833 --> 00:02:37,433
For Mother Mary.

43
00:02:37,483 --> 00:02:38,633
We always come.

44
00:02:38,683 --> 00:02:40,333
There are Christians...

45
00:02:40,383 --> 00:02:41,033
Yes.

46
00:02:41,133 --> 00:02:44,333
Muslims. All together.

47
00:02:47,033 --> 00:02:48,433
Is it the first time for you here?

48
00:02:49,583 --> 00:02:50,133
What's your name?

49
00:02:50,433 --> 00:02:51,433
Elizabeth.

50
00:02:52,033 --> 00:02:53,133
What does it mean for you?

51
00:02:53,713 --> 00:02:56,833
It's just like giving a devotion to Mother
Mary.

52
00:02:57,333 --> 00:03:00,433
She has given me a lot of blessings in my
life.

53
00:03:01,033 --> 00:03:01,983
Through Jesus Christ.

54
00:03:02,233 --> 00:03:03,933
So you are a Christian, of course.

55
00:03:04,583 --> 00:03:06,433
You are Christian. Yes.

56
00:03:06,933 --> 00:03:07,733
How old are you?

57
00:03:08,033 --> 00:03:08,833
Twenty-six.

58
00:03:09,233 --> 00:03:10,083
This is the first time here.

59
00:03:10,283 --> 00:03:11,933
Are you from Kerala?

60
00:03:14,633 --> 00:03:15,483
I'm from Malappuram.

61
00:03:18,083 --> 00:03:19,483
And for you, is it the first time?

62
00:03:19,533 --> 00:03:20,183
No.

63
00:03:20,683 --> 00:03:21,683
We walked on the beach.

64
00:03:22,333 --> 00:03:23,983
And now we're on the road.

65
00:03:24,633 --> 00:03:25,733
What does it mean for you?

66
00:03:25,933 --> 00:03:27,633
This is faith and belief.

67
00:03:27,833 --> 00:03:29,683
There are so many miracles happening
there.

68
00:03:31,733 --> 00:03:35,833
Those who take part in this find something
in it.

69
00:03:35,933 --> 00:03:37,233
Some happiness.

70
00:03:38,203 --> 00:03:39,983
And it's not only people walking.

71
00:03:40,433 --> 00:03:41,233
There are also those who don't walk.

72
00:03:41,903 --> 00:03:44,183
At the side of the road, with big pots and
glasses of water.

73
00:03:44,713 --> 00:03:46,883
They give food and drink to anyone passing
by.

74
00:03:47,483 --> 00:03:48,583
Without asking for anything in return.

75
00:03:49,433 --> 00:03:52,083
Some pray, some watch from their homes,
some offer water,

76
00:03:52,633 --> 00:03:53,383
and some are just curious.

77
00:03:56,833 --> 00:03:59,383
This was a stop inside, to drink and eat
something.

78
00:04:00,083 --> 00:04:02,783
Volunteers, women and men, devoted to the
cause,

79
00:04:04,823 --> 00:04:06,183
lending a hand.

80
00:04:12,783 --> 00:04:14,033
Truly a community coming together.

81
00:04:14,783 --> 00:04:18,683
Let's try to join them for a little while,
respecting the tradition.

82
00:04:19,643 --> 00:04:21,233
The sun rises and the road doesn't empty.

83
00:04:32,303 --> 00:04:33,633
The closer you get, the slower you go.

84
00:04:44,883 --> 00:04:45,633
We made it.

85
00:04:58,393 --> 00:05:00,933
Now that the whole pilgrimage is over.

86
00:05:02,633 --> 00:05:04,383
In Kerala, Christianity is ancient.

87
00:05:04,913 --> 00:05:08,683
Tradition says it arrived with the apostle
Thomas, in 52 AD.

88
00:05:10,733 --> 00:05:12,933
This church was rebuilt in 1584

89
00:05:14,033 --> 00:05:17,183
by an Italian Jesuit, Father Giacomo
Fenicio.

90
00:05:17,933 --> 00:05:20,833
Here they still call him Veluthachan,

91
00:05:21,233 --> 00:05:22,233
the white father.

92
00:05:22,443 --> 00:05:25,983
In 1647 a statue of Saint Sebastian
arrived from Milan.

93
00:05:26,873 --> 00:05:31,733
Since then Arthunkal has been a shrine, and in
January its feast brings people here from all over Kerala.

94
00:05:44,683 --> 00:05:47,683
It's boiling hot, really humid, you can
really feel it.

95
00:05:55,313 --> 00:05:56,933
I came to Kerala to listen to the people
who live here.

96
00:05:57,463 --> 00:06:01,033
I found myself inside 13 kilometres, next
to people I didn't know,

97
00:06:01,763 --> 00:06:03,133
who gave us something to drink without
asking for anything.

98
00:06:04,193 --> 00:06:06,133
Because travelling doesn't only mean
seeing new places.

99
00:06:06,743 --> 00:06:11,133
It also means stopping to listen to
stories we would never have known otherwise.

100
00:06:12,273 --> 00:06:14,683
The journey of Voci Vere, giving a voice
to those who need it most, continues.

101
00:06:15,433 --> 00:06:17,533
Follow me to discover the next stories.
